precept ContractorInvoiceSettlement

# A contractor invoice that bills labor at an hourly rate, then settles when the
# client remits payment. The shop logs hours worked against an agreed hourly rate;
# the labor charge is the rate times the worked time. The client's ledger is kept
# in USD, but a remittance may arrive in any currency — the remittance is recorded
# as-is, then governance decides whether it can be applied to the USD ledger. Only
# a remittance whose currency is USD may touch the balance; a foreign-currency
# remittance is held for the client to convert and resubmit.
#
# Two domain-typed mechanisms carry the model:
#   - Hourly billing as a temporal-denominator price. HourlyRate is a
#     `price in 'USD/hours'` (money per unit of time) and WorkedTime is a
#     `period of 'time'`. The product `HourlyRate * WorkedTime` cancels the
#     time denominator and resolves to `money in 'USD'` — the engine proves the
#     dimensional cancellation at compile time, so billing a rate against a
#     non-time quantity, or in the wrong currency, is structurally impossible.
#   - Open-payment governance via guard narrowing. Payment is an open `money`
#     (no declared currency) because the client can remit in any currency. The
#     apply transition guards `when Payment.currency == 'USD'`, which narrows the
#     open field to USD and lets it be added to the USD ledger; the unguarded
#     sibling row rejects a non-USD remittance. The narrowed assignment is proved
#     statically — a guard on the wrong currency would not discharge it.

# Identity
field InvoiceNumber as string optional maxlength 40
field ContractorName as string optional maxlength 200
field ClientName as string optional maxlength 200

# Labor billing — hourly rate as a temporal-denominator price; worked time as a
# calendar-relative period whose dimension is 'time'. HourlyRate is required once
# the invoice exists, but has no meaning while the invoice is still a draft, so it
# is omitted in Draft and first set at issuance.
field HourlyRate as price in 'USD/hours'
field WorkedTime as period of 'time' default '0 hours'

# Labor charge — derived from rate x time. The dimensional cancellation
# (price 'USD/hours' x period 'time' -> money 'USD') is enforced structurally;
# this computed field cannot be assigned and updates whenever its inputs change.
# Because it reads HourlyRate, it is likewise absent while in Draft.
field LaborCharge as money in 'USD' <- HourlyRate * WorkedTime

# Client ledger — denominated in USD. AmountApplied accumulates applied
# remittances; the outstanding balance is the labor charge less what's applied.
field AmountApplied as money in 'USD' default '0.00 USD' nonnegative
field OutstandingBalance as money in 'USD' <- LaborCharge - AmountApplied

# Remittance under governance — the open-currency payment the client sent. It is
# recorded as-is on RecordRemittance, then narrowed to USD (or rejected) on Apply.
field Payment as money optional
field RemittanceCurrencyOnRecord as currency optional
field SettlementNote as string optional

# Audit
field InvoiceLog as log of string

# Rules — applied payments can never exceed the labor charge billed. The rule
# reads LaborCharge, which is omitted while in Draft/Voided, so it is automatically
# scoped out of those lifecycle positions and enforced everywhere LaborCharge exists.
rule AmountApplied <= LaborCharge because "Applied payments {AmountApplied} cannot exceed the labor charge billed ({LaborCharge})"

# States
state Draft initial
state Issued
state RemittanceHeld
state Settled terminal
state Voided terminal

# HourlyRate (and therefore LaborCharge / OutstandingBalance) has no meaning in a
# draft or voided invoice — there is no agreed rate in those positions.
in Draft, Voided omit HourlyRate

# Editable window — the shop fills the invoice header and logs worked time in Draft.
in Draft modify InvoiceNumber, ContractorName, ClientName, WorkedTime editable

# State ensures
in Issued ensure InvoiceNumber is set because "An issued invoice must carry an invoice number"
in RemittanceHeld ensure Payment is set because "A held remittance must have a recorded payment amount"

# Events
event Issue(Rate as price in 'USD/hours')
on Issue ensure InvoiceNumber is set because "Invoice number is required before the invoice can be issued"
on Issue ensure ContractorName is set because "Contractor name is required before the invoice can be issued"
on Issue ensure WorkedTime.hours > 0 because "Worked time must be positive before billing — there is nothing to invoice for zero hours"

# A remittance arrives in an open currency. The host passes whatever the client
# actually paid; the precept records it, then governs whether it can be applied.
event RecordRemittance(Amount as money, Note as string optional)
event Apply
event Reissue
event Void(Reason as string notempty)

# Transitions

# Issue — the shop locks in the agreed hourly rate and bills the logged hours.
from Draft on Issue
    -> set HourlyRate = Issue.Rate
    -> append InvoiceLog "Issued"
    -> transition Issued

# Record a remittance — captured as-is into the open Payment field, in whatever
# currency the client actually sent. No currency judgment happens here.
from Issued on RecordRemittance
    -> set Payment = RecordRemittance.Amount
    -> set SettlementNote = if RecordRemittance.Note is set then RecordRemittance.Note else "Remittance received"
    -> append InvoiceLog "Remittance recorded"
    -> transition RemittanceHeld

# Apply — currency narrowing in action. The guard narrows the open Payment to USD,
# which lets it be added to the USD ledger; the assignment is proved statically.
# A USD remittance that fully covers the balance settles the invoice.
from RemittanceHeld on Apply when Payment is set and Payment.currency == 'USD' and AmountApplied + Payment >= LaborCharge
    -> set AmountApplied = LaborCharge
    -> set RemittanceCurrencyOnRecord = Payment.currency
    -> append InvoiceLog "Settled in full"
    -> transition Settled

# A USD remittance that covers only part of the balance is applied and the
# invoice returns to Issued to await the remainder.
from RemittanceHeld on Apply when Payment is set and Payment.currency == 'USD'
    -> set AmountApplied = AmountApplied + Payment
    -> set RemittanceCurrencyOnRecord = Payment.currency
    -> append InvoiceLog "Partial remittance applied"
    -> transition Issued

# Wrong currency: the open remittance is not USD — it cannot touch the USD ledger.
# The guard above did not narrow Payment to USD, so this row catches it.
from RemittanceHeld on Apply
    -> reject "Remittance is in {Payment.currency} — only USD remittances can be applied to this USD invoice. Convert and resubmit."

# Reissue — a held foreign-currency remittance is cleared so the client can resend
# in USD; the invoice returns to Issued awaiting a fresh remittance.
from RemittanceHeld on Reissue
    -> clear Payment
    -> append InvoiceLog "Remittance returned for currency conversion"
    -> transition Issued

# Void — the invoice is cancelled before settlement.
from Draft, Issued, RemittanceHeld on Void
    -> set SettlementNote = Void.Reason
    -> append InvoiceLog "Voided"
    -> transition Voided
